<name>Power Door Lock System</name>
<para id="RM00000200D007X" category="J" type-id="801QS" name-id="622Q2-00" from="200612">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>All doors do not lock or unlock with master switch or key-linked operation</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM00000200D007X_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000028J00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>The manual door lock/unlock request signal from the power window regulator master switch assembly is sent to the instrument panel junction block assembly (main body ECU) via LIN communication.</ptxt>
<ptxt>The manual door lock/unlock request signal from driver side key-linked operation is sent via a solid line to the instrument panel junction block assembly (main body ECU).</ptxt>
<ptxt>On receiving the door lock/unlock request signal, the instrument panel junction block assembly (main body ECU) operates the door lock motors of all seats to lock/unlock.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Some functions of the power door lock system use multiplex communication. First, follow "How to Proceed with Troubleshooting" and confirm that there is no malfunction in the communication system before proceeding with troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</content5>
</subpara>
